    "result_text": "The full build passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` derived field \u2014 `EMAIL` when the owner has an email, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nThe response DTO is generated from an OpenAPI spec and populated by a MapStruct mapper, so I followed the existing pattern for the other derived fields (`displayName`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` property to the `Owner` response schema (typed as a plain string, matching how the controlled-vocabulary `locality` field is declared).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(contactPreference(owner))\")` and a small single-responsibility default method computing `EMAIL`/`PHONE`, reusing the same blank-safe email check already used by `membershipLevel`.\n\nNo responder/function or persistence changes were needed since `GET /api/owners/{id}` already flows through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`. Both new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass.",
